WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.309
2017 is the year that Canada celebrates 150
years of existence.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:22.680
The 
specific day of their ‘birthday’ was the

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:28.090
1st of July, so, well, belated happy birthday
Canada…

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:35.330
And well, dear viewer, 150 years of existence
is not the only matter that we should be congratulating

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.330
Canada on...

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.290
The country reached its 150th anniversary
in great shape.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:44.400
Because, well, if there’s something we can
say about Canada right now it’s that the

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.280
&nbsp;country is certainly ‘in vogue’.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:56.610
And yes, Canada is also the homeland of many
celebrities that we all know well.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:06.510
But recently there’s been one celebrity
who has been put in the international political

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.510
spotlight.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.550
We are talking of course of Justin…

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:15.420
No, no, NO, not that Justin...

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.289
We meant, this one: Trudeau.

00:01:17.289 --> 00:01:21.590
Justin Trudeau!

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:25.840
Canada has reached its 150th anniversary as
one of the richest countries in the world,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.880
with a top-notch quality of life, as well
as being one of the most admired countries

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.840
on Earth.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:32.840
Not bad, right?

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:33.929
So now you might be wondering…

00:01:33.929 --> 00:01:35.429
What is the cause of all of this?

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:39.880
What are the main achievements that Canada
is celebrating after 150 years?

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.569
And importantly, Is there any dark side to
Canada?

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:46.970
Well, we are going to answer all of these
questions in this video, but first let’s

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.390
get some perspective...

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.740
[THE GREAT TRANSFORMATION]

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:57.799
You might not have heard much about Canada
recently, but we can certainly say they are

00:01:57.799 --> 00:01:59.159
no ordinary country...

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:03.530
In fact, Canada is the second biggest country
in the world with it’s territory covering

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.149
six different time zones!

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:07.590
And… guess which country has the most coastline
in the world?

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.709
Well, no prizes if you guessed Canada!

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:14.930
Of course, as all regular VisualPolitik viewers
already know, neither the size of a country’s

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:21.130
surface nor its coastline determines its wealth
or how many opportunities its citizens have.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.290
So then…

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.680
What’s really behind the success of Canada?

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.021
Well, one key factor here is the disastrous
years that Canada had at the late 80s and

00:02:31.021 --> 00:02:32.990
early 90s.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:39.580
( In this period of time Canada suffered economic
stagnations and several crises to the point

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:45.440
that in 1995 the Wall Street Journal dubbed
Canada as “an honorary member of the Third

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.670
World” due to their inability to control
their governmental accounts.)

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:54.090
Since then, as you can see, things have changed
enormously…

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:59.140
Canada really knew how to play to their strengths
and get rid of what was hurting them.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.730
And especially, above all, Canadians have
understood the importance of the meaning of

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:08.510
these two words: COMPETITIVENESS and INTEGRATION.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:13.200
After those disastrous years of the 80s and
90s, Canadians realised that before thinking

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.980
about spending it is essential to think about
creating.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:23.250
And they realised that in order to do that
they needed investment, businesses, and trade...

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.230
a great deal of trade.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:34.190
Well… as it was said, so it was done.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.800
Today Canada is the 7th freest economy in
the world.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.370
But if we’re talking about freedom then
we can’t just talk about the economic side

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.370
of things.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:48.230
The Fraser Institute publishes every year
the “Human Freedom Index”, which measures

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.610
both the economic and civil freedoms that
people enjoy.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:55.040
Quite simple, it measures what we can do,
and what we can’t.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.660
Well, so according to their research Canada
is the 6th freest country on Earth.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:04.750
To give you a better idea of how this compares
to some other countries: the US ranks 23rd,

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.510
Italy 28th, and Japan ranks 32nd.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:14.730
Maybe the answer to this is in the strong
decentralization the country has.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:20.030
Canada is divided into 10 provinces and 3
territories that have so many unique regulations

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:25.180
that in 2017 they had to sign a free trade
agreement among them...

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:31.889
“New interprovincial trade deal expected
to add billions to economy - The Globe and

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:33.780
Mail”
The decentralization is enormous and it has

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:38.069
traditionally resulted in higher costs for
those companies that don’t operate in a

00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:43.979
single region but in several different regions,
with each region having different regulations.

00:04:43.979 --> 00:04:50.629
“In Ontario petrol must be at least 5% ethanol;
Manitoba insists on an 8.5% blend”.

00:04:50.629 --> 00:04:52.740
The Economist.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:56.990
The positive side of this is that this has
worked as a counterweight to the federal government,

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:00.930
and has encouraged them to make pro-citizen
policies, and that’s something that has

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:02.639
driven good public policies.

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:07.190
Anyway, this new agreement is has been created
in order to beat all these surprising obstacles.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:11.389
Further, as we talked about in a previous
video, there’s also the Canadian bet on

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:13.020
multiculturalism.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.800
And hey, let us be rather frank here: nowadays
this country is one of the best examples of

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:25.460
integration in the entire world.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.740
THE CANADIAN MOSAIC

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.820
But, what’s all this “Canadian multiculturalism”
about?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:37.020
Well, basically it consists on accepting that
cultural diversity is not a threat but an

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.490
asset and a source of opportunities.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:44.490
Now, of course, this multiculturalism is always
subordinate to a core set of values such as

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:49.919
democracy, rule of law and equality for all
people.

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:54.280
This means, in order to be Canadian and be
welcomed to their country you don’t have

00:05:54.280 --> 00:06:01.740
to replace your culture with any other, you
just have to accept and commit to those core

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:02.740
values.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:06.419
Look, Canada has one of the largest populations
of immigrants in the world.

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:09.759
1 out of every 5 Canadians weren’t born
in Canada.

00:06:09.759 --> 00:06:14.770
And for some cities, like Toronto, this figure
goes up to 50%, or even higher...

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:20.099
And it seems that it will be even higher in
the future, because every year more than 300,000

00:06:20.099 --> 00:06:24.979
new immigrants come to this country - one
of the highest immigration rates in the world.

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:27.070
And, do you know what?

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.160
It’s no problem at all.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:37.819
Yes, as we said before, immigration in Canada
is not free, there’s a system based on 3

00:06:37.819 --> 00:06:45.409
fundamental pillars: points, family reunification,
and refugees.

00:06:45.409 --> 00:06:50.870
The most important one of these is the point
based system that exists to grant people residence

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:51.919
or work permits.

00:06:51.919 --> 00:06:56.800
It considers things like having a job offer
(the most important thing) or also having

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:01.370
a degree, or being able to speak English.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.740
And do you want to know the results?

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.919
Well, almost 80% of Canadians think that immigration
is good for the economy, something that is

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:13.930
not so strange when you consider that all
the statistics show that immigrants, the “brand-new

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:19.309
Canadians”, are more educated, work more
hours, create more businesses, and draw less

00:07:19.309 --> 00:07:22.589
dollars from social programmes.

00:07:22.589 --> 00:07:26.080
Does Canada have rules about immigration?

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.169
Certainly.

00:07:27.169 --> 00:07:34.449
But this sort of welcoming culture focused
on integration is rare to find...

00:07:34.449 --> 00:07:42.839
In fact, since 1977 every Canadian citizen
can hold any other nationality without restriction.

00:07:42.839 --> 00:07:46.860
So when someone emigrates to Canada, and after
some years obtain their Canadian passport,

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.749
they don’t have to renounce their previous
nationality.

00:07:49.749 --> 00:07:58.759
BUT, if something might perfectly show Canada’s
spirit, it’s Prime Minister Justin Trudeau.

00:07:58.759 --> 00:08:13.069
JUSTIN TRUDEAU, A POLITICAL STAR

00:08:13.069 --> 00:08:18.430
Justin Trudeau took office in 2015, almost
by surprise and at just 44 years of age.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:23.020
Today he is one of the most popular politicians
in the world, and that’s true in Canada

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.020
as well.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.310
This is something that polls clearly show…

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:32.110
A recent survey made by Abacus Data on the
leadership of the Prime Minister shows that

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:38.960
70% of Canadians are confident that Trudeau
will manage in a good way relations with allies.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:45.110
63% trust his decision making responsibility,
and 62% believe that his decisions will be

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:46.110
good.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:52.520
I mean, how many politicians around the world
would like approval ratings like that?!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:57.620
However, Trudeau is not a typical politician,
not at all.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:02.000
The Prime Minister of Canada has put on the
table a programme, and a form of government,

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.830
that’s quite different from what’s typically
being used.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:09.350
A look at his cabinet is a realistic sample
of Canada’s reality:

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:16.519
15 of the 30 ministers are women.

00:09:16.519 --> 00:09:23.430
We can find a Bosnia and Afghanistan veteran,
a former volunteer in Niger, ex-business executives

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:27.880
or even some ministers who are sikhs, - a
religion native to Punjab, an Indian state.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:35.430
The latest addition, by the way, has been
Ahmed Hussen, a Somali who arrived to Canada

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.600
as a refugee at 16 years old and that now
is the Minister of Immigration.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.290
Pretty amazing, right?

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.699
Trudeau’s political priorities are international
as his cabinet...

00:09:44.699 --> 00:09:49.040
One of Canada’s government key challenges
is to boost trade among nations.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:52.110
Pay attention to their Foreign Affairs Minister:

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.360
“Rising trade barriers hurt the people they
are intended to help.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:00.199
They curb growth, stifle innovation and kill
employment.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.420
This is a lesson we should learn from history”.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:03.420
Chrystia Freeland, Global Affairs Minister
of Canada.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.389
That is why Trudeau wants to sign a free trade
agreement even with China.

00:10:07.389 --> 00:10:11.800
Secondly, unlike other governments, Trudeau
doesn’t just reject protectionism but he

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:17.130
wants to stimulate a productive change with
artificial intelligence and automation.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.589
Why hinder technology?

00:10:18.589 --> 00:10:22.610
If there’s something we’ve seen as history
has progressed it is that technology improves

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:27.120
people’s lives and creates more jobs.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:33.160
It might seems like something that isn’t
too complicated to do, but the reality is

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:37.610
that there are not many world leaders who
defend this pro-technology position.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:41.199
Talking about jobs going away is not exactly
a popular line…

00:10:41.199 --> 00:10:45.240
The other great challenge, and maybe the key
value of Trudeau’s government is their bet

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:49.690
on boosting civil rights and turning Canada
into an international example of how this

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:50.690
should be done.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:55.089
Take a look on the power of this picture,
Trudeau has become the first Primer Minister

00:10:55.089 --> 00:10:58.019
to lead a LGBTQ pride parade.

00:10:58.019 --> 00:11:02.100
There’s also their most recently released
programme: Canada’s Feminist International

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.100
Assistance Policy.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.389
Yep, you heard right.

00:11:04.389 --> 00:11:07.970
Trudeau’s government didn’t hesitate to
declare itself as feminist, and among other

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:11.709
things, they have decided to focus most of
their international cooperation budget on

00:11:11.709 --> 00:11:14.810
pushing women’s rights where they are most
needed.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:19.160
Now, this is just a symbol, but sometimes
symbols are important...

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:23.009
Other symbols and gestures are his position
towards Syrian refugees.

00:11:23.009 --> 00:11:47.160
Pay close attention to this speech:
Until now, 40,000 syrian refugees 

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:52.319
have arrived Canada, almost half of them thanks
to the sponsorship of Canadian citizens that

00:11:52.319 --> 00:11:57.089
have committed to be responsible for the wellness
of these people.

00:11:57.089 --> 00:11:59.839
A great example of solidarity.

00:11:59.839 --> 00:12:05.620
But hey, because it’s one thing is being
generous and kind, and quite another to be

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:06.620
naive.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.069
Consider this: the Canadian government has
announced its intention to increase military

00:12:10.069 --> 00:12:16.800
spending more than 70% from now until 2024,
in order to create a more agile and modern

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:20.750
Armed Forces.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:26.269
Trade, doors opened to technology, integration,
civil rights, security…

00:12:26.269 --> 00:12:29.540
All these things don’t sound bad at all,
right?

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:33.649
Especially, if you consider that this government
understands that before starting to discuss

00:12:33.649 --> 00:12:36.540
spending, you have to talk about wealth creation.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:41.190
Well, that’s how Canada has reached its
150 anniversary…

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.100
Everything bloody marvellous, right?

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.070
WELL, WAIT A SECOND…

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.070
Not exactly...

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.269
There are some shadows…

00:12:47.269 --> 00:12:51.670
But we’re going to leave the “dark side
of Canada” for another video video.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:56.310
Don’t think that we are going to just talk
about how wonderful and rosy things are…

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.230
Oh no, not at all.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:02.329
Well, so, don’t forget to subscribe to our
channel so you don’t miss that video and

00:13:02.329 --> 00:13:04.870
hear the other side of the story.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:08.199
And now we want to ask you, what’s your
opinion on Trudeau?

00:13:08.199 --> 00:13:12.730
You can leave us your comments below and also
by clicking on the survey on the screen now.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.980
Also, don’t forget to check out our friends
at the Reconsider Media Podcast - they provided

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:19.019
the vocals in this episode that were not mine!

00:13:19.019 --> 00:13:20.949
And as always, thanks for watching!

